  "method": {
    "block_timing": "continuous run: the interval between the first accepted samples of consecutive blocks is the block II (256 intervals for 257 blocks, the first 256 blocks); fill is the first accepted input to the first valid output and tail the last accepted input to the last output beat",
    "capture": "the continuous run writes every captured output (+capture_file) in the .hex format; the SHA-256 of its valid-window records must equal expected_hex_sha256, independently of the testbench comparator. Records outside the window are declared block padding: recorded, not compared",
    "comparison": "exact stored codes at absolute index received*SPC + lane + latency_samples; a mismatch reports index, expected and captured code",
    "continuous": "valid_i and ready_i held high; asserts latency_cycles from the first accepted input to the first valid output, measures II from accepted-input edges",
    "drain": "valid_i stops after the declared accepted count; outputs drain under ready_i=1 with a bounded timeout and a check for undeclared extra emissions",
    "midtraffic_reset": "asynchronous reset after an accepted prefix, then the robust run restarts at record 0",
    "robustness": "seeded source bubbles and sink stalls plus a post-input tail stall; the testbench fails unless bubbles, sink stalls and DUT ready_o backpressure all occur",
    "vcd": "+vcd_file dumps the ports and the engine control state over the continuous run; the engine enters LOAD, RUN, EMIT and DRAIN once per block, so every block is covered only if each count equals the block count. The dump stays in the build directory; the evidence keeps its size and the hash of its value changes"
  },
